    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "These two properties are nestled at the end of a quiet road and 1.5 km to Ballyvaughan village, and are a must see for those wishing to find a west of Ireland bolt hole or investment property, on the coast and the Burren in Co. Clare.\n\nBoth properties are sold in one lot, are in need of refurbishment and repair and offer an exceptional opportunity to create a spacious dwelling on an impressive 7.96 acres. \n\nThe larger property although maintaining a modern day facade contains some surprisingly traditional features, e,g, a parlour with an antique fireplace and shuttered windows, and throughout the house some interesting dressers, cabinets, and an old range \nits accommodation extends to1,680 sq. ft. and contains an entrance hallway, sitting room, kitchenette, shower room, w.c, dining room, sun room, five bedrooms and a bathroom\n\nThe smaller property is a cottage, blending harmoniously within the surrounding natural landscape. Its accommodation extends to approx. 484 sq. ft. and includes an entrance porch, sitting room, kitchenette, 2 bedrooms and a bathroom\n\nBoth sit on a generous plot providing privacy and a wealth of potential for gardening enthusiasts, or simply enjoying the great outdoors.\n\nWhether you dream of keeping horses, cultivating a vegetable garden, or simply enjoying the peace and quiet of rural living, this property provides the perfect canvas. \n\nLoughrask itself is a delightful area within County Clare, known for its scenic landscapes and friendly community. The village is ideally situated for those who appreciate outdoor activities and cultural experiences. Nearby, you can explore the Burren National Park, providing unique limestone landscapes and a wealth of flora and fauna.\n\nLocal amenities in the surrounding towns include charming pubs, restaurants, artisan shops, where you can sample local produce and crafts. \n\nFor families, there are good schools in the vicinity, and the community spirit in Loughrask is strong, with regular events and activities that bring neighbours together. The towns of Ennis and Kinvara are a short drive away, offeringi a wider range of shopping, dining, and entertainment options, as well as excellent transport links to Limerick and Galway.\n\nViewing is highly recommended"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Main House\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.3m (10'10\") x 2.6m (8'6\")\nThis room has carpet flooring. NW facing window. WHB\n\nHallway - 12.2m (40'0\") x 1m (3'3\")\nThis area has tiled floor\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.3m (10'10\") x 2.6m (8'6\")\nThis room has carpet flooring. NE facing window\n\nShower/Wet Room - 2.7m (8'10\") x 1.8m (5'11\")\nThis area is tiled floor to ceiling and contains shower, w.c, w.h.b and heated towel rail.\n\nW.C - 2.7m (8'10\") x 0.9m (2'11\")\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.8m (12'6\") x 3.6m (11'10\")\nThis room has carpet flooring and North East facing windows\n\nSitting Room - 4.7m (15'5\") x 3.7m (12'2\")\nThis room has solid wood original flooring, double aspect South West and North West facing windows, antique mantle and fireplace with mirrored over mantle unit with shelving\n\nDining Room - 3.6m (11'10\") x 3.7m (12'2\")\nThis area has original solid wooden floors, antique fireplace and S.W facing windows.\n\nInternal Hallway - 4.6m (15'1\") x 1.2m (3'11\")\nThis area has tiled flooring\n\nLiving Room - 4.8m (15'9\") x 3.65m (12'0\")\nThis room has tiled flooring, old style dresser unit, staircase to the first floor\n\nStore Room/Office - 3m (9'10\") x 2.4m (7'10\")\nThis area has wood effect laminate flooring and South East facing windows\n\nKitchenette - 3m (9'10\") x 2.4m (7'10\")\nThis area has tiled flooring and fitted kitchen units\n\nBack Porch - 1.2m (3'11\") x 1.4m (4'7\")\nThis area has South East facing windows\n\nSun Room - 7.5m (24'7\") x 2.4m (7'10\")\nThis area has triple aspect windows\n\nOffice - 3.2m (10'6\") x 2.8m (9'2\")\nThis room is located on the first floor and has carpet flooring and the access to the attic is located here\n\nChalet\n\nEntrance Porch - 1m (3'3\") x 0.9m (2'11\")\nThis area has Liscannor stone flooring\n\nInternal Hallway - 2.4m (7'10\") x 1.1m (3'7\")\nThis area has Liscannor Stone Flooring\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.7m (12'2\") x 2.5m (8'2\")\nThis room has wood effect laminate flooring, double aspect windows, t&g pine ceilings and w.h.b\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.7m (8'10\") x 2.4m (7'10\")\nThis room has carpet flooring, w.h.b, fitted wardrobes, S.E facing windows and t&g pine ceilings\n\nLiving Room - 4.8m (15'9\") x 3.5m (11'6\")\nThis area has Liscannor stone flooring, solid fuel storage and electric storage heater, valuted t&g pine ceiling\n\nInternal Hallway - 1.1m (3'7\") x 1.1m (3'7\")\nThis area has carpet flooring, N.E facing windows\n\nShower Room - 1.55m (5'1\") x 1.4m (4'7\")\nThis area has tiled floor to ceiling, corner shower unit, w.c and w.h.b\n\nKitcheneete\nThis area has fitted kitchen units with wall shelving, s.s sink with mixer tap.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
